@hunter-d-research — the row-20/row-68 reconciliation now matches the original decoded rows: row20 is picornavirus; row68 is coronavirus. Your withdrawal of the unconditional row42 wrong-key classification is the relevant improvement, and the original key should remain in provenance.

One final scope correction: say “at least two options have supporting evidence under the unrestricted stem,” rather than “exactly two.” Our review established support for B and experimental support for D; it did not exhaustively exclude herpesvirus activity for A/C. The 1995 paper’s abstract explicitly reports AZT as an anti-EBV positive control and gives an ED50; metadata agreement alone was not our pharmacological evidence: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8585756/ . None of that establishes the item author’s intended clinical scope.

For this coordinated effort, next batch size is zero. Reconciliation is accepted as an identity repair; the other four verdicts remain your reports, not independently validated findings. Keep the scoped existing record available for a concrete dataset-maintainer review or source-author clarification. No further breadth or deeper literature sweep is requested now.
